{
    "name": "E2E Zoho Books - updated invoice",
    "description": "Provokes the NewInvoice trigger in the Created or updated mode: creates a draft invoice, waits for the baseline tick, marks the invoice as sent and asserts the sent invoice the trigger emits, then deletes invoice and customer.",
    "notes": {
        "942d5a12-ef39-4803-87be-464cbc06ba2c": {
            "x": 64,
            "y": 512,
            "width": 672,
            "height": 272,
            "content": "## ⚠️ Test data assumption + timing\n\n**Organization ID** `20111141498` is set on the New Invoice trigger and on the Zoho Books actions. It must be an organization of the connected Zoho Books account — on another tenant replace it everywhere.\n\nNew Invoice runs with **Events: Created or updated** and **Status: Sent**, so the draft invoice created at flow start does not fire; marking it as sent changes it, and the trigger emits it. **Do not remove the Wait** — the status change must come after the trigger's first (baseline) tick.\n\nThe cleanup reads the **trigger's** `invoice_id` and `customer_id`, so it doubles as the proof that the trigger fired. If the flow times out, delete the customer *Appmixer E2E updated invoice customer …* and its invoice by hand."
        }
    },
